ame year\nGet Started\nRequest Info\nApply Now\nApplication Requirements\nApplication Forms\nYou must submit a completed application.\nApplication Fee\n$75 Application fee.\nThe application fee is waived for current BC students, McNair Scholars, IRT participants, active JVC members, Americorps volunteers, Teach for America corps members, and active duty military. Current undergraduate applicants, for whom the fee would constitute a serious hardship, may request a waiver.\nStandardized Tests\nThe GRE General Test and Physics Subject Test are recommended but not required. Submitting GRE scores may be advantageous in many situations by providing additional information that is not delivered by other application materials.\nTranscripts\nTranscripts of all previous academic work.\nRecommendations\nThree letters of recommendation are required.\nTOEFL or IELTS\nApplicants whose first language is not English must take the Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL) or the International English Language Testing System (IELTS) exam. This requirement is waived for those whose highest degree is from an English speaking country.\nStatement of Purpose\nDescribe why you are pursuing this degree and how it aligns with your interests and goals.\nBack To Top\nDepartment of Physics\nHiggins Hall 335\n617-552-3575\nphysics@bc.edu\nMorrissey College of Arts and Sciences\nGasson Hall\n140 Commonwealth Avenue\nChestnut Hill, MA 02467\nContact\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nDepartments\nArt, Art History, and Film\nBiology\nChemistry\nClassical Studies\nCommunication\nComputer Science\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nEconomics\nEngineering\nEnglish\nGerman Studies\nHistory\nMathematics\nMusic\nPhilosophy\nPhysics\nPolitical Science\nPsychology\nRomance Languages and Literatures\nSlavic & Eastern Languages and Literatures\nSociology\nTheatre\nTheology\nGiving to Morrissey\nGive to Physics\nFaculty Resources\nApply\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFollow Us\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYoutube\nAccessibil